    "q-355226": {
      "dom_id": "step-q355226",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "| $t$ | $h(t)$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $-4$ | $5$ |\n| $-2$ | $-1$ |\n| $0$ | $-3$ |\n| $3$ | $2$ |\n| $5$ | $4$ |\n\nThe table above gives values of a function $h$ on the set $T=\\{-4,-2,0,3,5\\}.$ Compute the following:\n\n${max}_{t\\in T}h(t)=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{t\\in T}h(t)=$\n{{field-2}}\n\n${min}_{t\\in T}h(t)=$\n{{field-3}}\n\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{t\\in T}h(t)=$\n{{field-4}}",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that \n\n- ${max}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is the maximum output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that maximum output occurs.\n\nOn the other hand,\n\n- ${min}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is the minimum output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that minimum output occurs.\n\nThe output values are $5,-1,-3,2,$ and $4.$ The maximum output is $5$ (at $t=-4$), and the minimum output is $-3$ (at $t=0$). \n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{max}_{t\\in T}h(t) & =5 \\\\ \\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{t\\in T}h(t) & =-4 \\\\ {min}_{t\\in T}h(t) & =-3 \\\\ \\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{t\\in T}h(t) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
