    "q-355224": {
      "dom_id": "step-q355224",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "| $t$ | $h(t)$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $-5$ | $1$ |\n| $-3$ | $3$ |\n| $0$ | $-2$ |\n| $1$ | $5$ |\n| $2$ | $-4$ |\n\nThe table above gives values of a function $h$ on the set $T=\\{-5,-3,0,1,2\\}.$ Compute the following:\n\n${max}_{t\\in T}h(t)=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{t\\in T}h(t)=$\n{{field-2}}\n\n${min}_{t\\in T}h(t)=$\n{{field-3}}\n\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{t\\in T}h(t)=$\n{{field-4}}",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that \n\n- ${max}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is the maximum output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that maximum output occurs.\n\nOn the other hand,\n\n- ${min}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is the minimum output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that minimum output occurs.\n\nThe output values are $1,3,-2,5,$ and $-4.$ The maximum output is $5$ (at $t=1$), and the minimum output is $-4$ (at $t=2$). \n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{max}_{t\\in T}h(t) & =5 \\\\ \\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{t\\in T}h(t) & =1 \\\\ {min}_{t\\in T}h(t) & =-4 \\\\ \\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{t\\in T}h(t) & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
