    "q-355232": {
      "dom_id": "step-q355232",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14221505/assets/af893cca4e4fe3d4b62f02997fa799dec3e35fbe8942d2d3c90d2eeb6bbc919c.png)\n\nLet $T=\\{-3,-2,0,1,3\\}.$ The graph above shows the value of $g(x)$ for each $x\\in T.$ Assuming that all the dots have integer coordinates, compute the following:\n\n${max}_{x\\in T}g(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in T}g(x)=$\n{{field-2}}\n\n${min}_{x\\in T}g(x)=$\n{{field-3}}\n\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in T}g(x)=$\n{{field-4}}",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that \n\n- ${max}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is the maximum output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that maximum output occurs.\n\nOn the other hand,\n\n- ${min}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is the minimum output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that minimum output occurs.\n\nFrom the graph, \n\n- the highest point is at $(0,4),$ so ${max}_{x\\in T}g(x)=4$ and $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in T}g(x)=0,$ and\n\n- the lowest point is at $(-2,-1),$ so ${min}_{x\\in T}g(x)=-1$ and $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in T}g(x)=-2.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
