    "q-355243": {
      "dom_id": "step-q355243",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14221505/assets/7bc88ac3502f2842e05dd48eb6635b2c54c6392ec6f6427e77528732a3180db8.png)\n\nLet $T=\\{1,2,3,4,5\\}.$ The graph above shows the value of $h(x)$ for each $x\\in T.$ Assuming that all the dots have integer coordinates, compute the following:\n\n${max}_{x\\in T}h(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in T}h(x)=$\n{{field-2}}\n\n${min}_{x\\in T}h(x)=$\n{{field-3}}\n\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in T}h(x)=$\n{{field-4}}",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that \n\n- ${max}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is the maximum output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that maximum output occurs.\n\nOn the other hand,\n\n- ${min}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is the minimum output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that minimum output occurs.\n\nFrom the graph, \n\n- the highest point is at $(2,4),$ so ${max}_{x\\in T}h(x)=4$ and $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in T}h(x)=2,$ and\n\n- the lowest point is at $(5,-2),$ so ${min}_{x\\in T}h(x)=-2$ and $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in T}h(x)=5.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
