    "q-355242": {
      "dom_id": "step-q355242",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14221505/assets/ab745b7220264fbf24032104e9ae60d4ffe0b7a58ce1d9a88d1d16ab4c23f9cc.png)\n\nLet $T=\\{-2,-1,0,1\\}.$ The graph above shows the value of $g(x)$ for each $x\\in T.$ Assuming that all the dots have integer coordinates, compute the following:\n\n${max}_{x\\in T}g(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in T}g(x)=$\n{{field-2}}\n\n${min}_{x\\in T}g(x)=$\n{{field-3}}\n\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in T}g(x)=$\n{{field-4}}",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that \n\n- ${max}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is the maximum output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that maximum output occurs.\n\nOn the other hand,\n\n- ${min}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is the minimum output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that minimum output occurs.\n\nFrom the graph, \n\n- the highest point is at $(-1,5),$ so ${max}_{x\\in T}g(x)=5$ and $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in T}g(x)=-1,$ and\n\n- the lowest point is at $(0,1),$ so ${min}_{x\\in T}g(x)=1$ and $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in T}g(x)=0.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
